# Works Content

## Page structure

Every work's `content.md` follows this layout:

```
[HI](../../)  ||  [WORKS](../../works/)  ||  [BLOG](../../writings/)  ||  [TALKS](../../talks/)  ||  [PRESS](../../press/)

# Title of the Work

Year: YYYY  
Type: medium, duration/dimensions

---

[description paragraphs — see the "writing-artwork-descriptions" skill]

[embeds, images, or links as needed]
```

- **Title** is the `# heading` — the source of truth for the URL slug and listings.
- **Year** and **Type** are metadata lines immediately after the title, each ending with two trailing spaces for a line break.
- The `---` rule separates metadata from body content.
- Bare YouTube URLs become embedded players; `[text](url)` stays a plain link.
- **Image paths must use `./` prefix:** `![alt](./filename.webp)`, not `![alt](filename.webp)`.

## Listing table

`works/content.md` is manually maintained. Each new work gets a row:

```
| [Title](./slug-folder/) | YYYY | medium, duration/dimensions |
```

Keep rows in **reverse chronological order** (newest first).

For external links (no local work subpage), use an HTML anchor with preview metadata so hover previews still work:

```
| <a href="https://example.com/work" data-preview="https://cdn.example.com/work.webp">Title</a> | YYYY | medium |
```

If needed, add `data-preview-tiny` for a dedicated blur placeholder.

**Do not “fix” this mix.** HTML anchors inside the Markdown table are intentional. Never rewrite them into plain Markdown links (or strip `data-preview`) without asking first — that silently breaks hover previews.

## Adding a new work

1. Generate folder ID: `openssl rand -hex 16`
2. Create folder: `works/{title-slug}-{id}/`
3. Add `content.md` with the structure above
4. Add `preview.webp` for the hover preview on the listing page
5. Run `python3 optimize-images.py --run` to generate `preview-tiny.webp`
6. Add a row to `works/content.md`
7. Run `python3 update-subpages.py`

## Descriptions

When writing or editing the description paragraphs, use the **writing-artwork-descriptions** skill for voice, structure, and length guidelines.
